==English==

===Etymology===
{{bf|en|micromanagement}}, equivalent to {{af|en|micro-|manage}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-us-micromanage.ogg|a=US}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|ambitransitive}} To [[manage]], [[direct]], or [[control]] a person, group, or system to an unnecessary level of [[detail]] or [[precision]].
#: {{ux|en|The employees complained that their boss was '''micromanaging''' when she insisted that they account for their time in fifteen-minute intervals.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2022 November 30|author=Cara Murphy|title=A new mindset for GBR|journal=RAIL|issue=971|page=44|text=As GBR is intended to operate at arm's length from government while also being responsible for implementing a 30-year strategy, it is hoped that the industry will be less '''micro-managed''' by ministers and officials at both the DfT and within the Treasury.}}